msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "DESCRIPTION"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The B<sigwait>()  function suspends execution of the calling thread until "
"one of the signals specified in the signal set I<set> becomes pending.  For "
"a signal to become pending, it must first be blocked with "
"B<sigprocmask>(2).  The function accepts the signal (removes it from the "
"pending list of signals), and returns the signal number in I<sig>."
msgstr ""
"La fonction B<sigwait>()  suspend l'exécution du thread appelant jusqu'à ce "
"que l'un des signaux indiqués dans l'ensemble de signaux I<set> soit en "
"attente. Pour qu'un signal se mette en attente, il doit d'abord être bloqué "
"par B<sigprocmask>(2). La fonction accepte le signal (le supprime de la "
"liste des signaux en attente), et retourne le numéro du signal dans I<sig>."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The operation of B<sigwait>()  is the same as B<sigwaitinfo>(2), except that:"
msgstr ""
"L'action de B<sigwait>()  est identique à celle de B<sigwaitinfo>(2), "
"excepté que\\ :"

#. type: IP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[bu]"
msgstr "-"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"B<sigwait>()  returns only the signal number, rather than a I<siginfo_t> "
"structure describing the signal."
msgstr ""
"B<sigwait>()  ne retourne que le numéro du signal et pas la structure "
"I<siginfo_t> décrivant le signal."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The return values of the two functions are different."
msgstr "Les valeurs de retour des deux fonctions sont différentes."

#. type: SH
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "RETURN VALUE"
